Subject: [PATCH 2/3] docs: record the Commit 5b resolution, oracle acceptance
 and the first fair MPC row

The oracle gate passes on seed block 262000: 5/5 completed with zero truth
violations, equivalent delta-v 1.51-2.58 m/s, mean force 0.70-1.71 N, worst
normalised margin +0.148, worst FOV margin +0.710 rad, 159.5-239.5 s, zero
actuator saturation.

Pure MPC h10 with a fixed target-frame setpoint, measured on the same code and
the same seed, does not complete: it locks onto the rotating setpoint within
20 s, pays the co-rotation bias continuously from 16 m, and is still crawling
at 7.66 m when the 300 s cap ends the episode. Equivalent delta-v 5.07 m/s
against the oracle's 1.51, and that is a lower bound because the episode was
truncated rather than finished. It is neither slow (41 ms mean, 50 ms p95,
0.41x/0.50x of the control period, zero QP fallback) nor unsafe (zero
violations, worst normalised margin +0.371) -- the defect is that the cheap
path needs a 119 s timing decision and no real-time horizon can see it.

PRECAPTURE_TASK_SPEC is updated to the V0.2 semantics it has been running for
two commits (6 m latch, 1.20 m/s outer limit plus the radial braking envelope,
the withdrawn 14-8 m transition band) and now states the tumble rate the whole
task rests on.

